    "q-126895": {
      "dom_id": "step-q126895",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14184009/assets/0db447407835f74476edd20ed5327ff3cc570905f744bbc6c29a66926913ecb5.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{∂D}(1-4y)\\,dx+(2+5x)\\,dy,$ where $D$ is the annular region shown above.",
      "worked_solution": "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=1-4y$ and $Q(x,y)=2+5x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-4,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}dx+x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5-(-4))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}9\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =9\\,\\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =9\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2}-\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}) \\\\  & =9\\cdot 5\\pi  \\\\  & =45\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
